# Layout

This file is the single technical reference for the scroll rules.
`knowledge-base/responsive/responsive.mdc` and `knowledge-base/ux/single-screen.mdc`
state the rule and refer here; the `<main>` implementation details live in the
comment inside `components/layout/app-layout.tsx`.

- Favor a contained interface — no global page scroll on dashboard pages; other
  pages may use the page scroll only when the content genuinely requires it.

- Use a container only on large screens.

- Remove the container on medium and small screens.

- ## Page Types and Scroll Behavior

### Dashboard and Detail pages

- At `md+`, the page MUST NOT create or allow page-level vertical scrolling.
- At `md+`, internal component scrolling is allowed when the component
  content requires it.
- Below `md`, page-level vertical scrolling is allowed.
- Below `md`, internal component scrolling MUST NOT be used.
- On mobile, overflowing content MUST remain reachable through page-level
  scrolling.

### Other pages

- Page-level vertical scrolling is allowed when the content genuinely
  requires it.
- Internal component scrolling may be used when appropriate.
- Avoid unnecessary nested scrolling.